<title>RUSSIA: Fifth Russia sugar beet content falls to 11.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Fifth Russia sugar beet content falls to 11.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's fifth sugar beet test, and the season's third for sugar content, showed a sugar content level of 11.6 percent from 12.0 percent at the same time last year, the Rossakhsvyokla sugar beet producers' association said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data:  </p>
<p>					    RUSSIAN SUGAR BEET TESTING</p>
<p>					 5th 1997 test     Year-ago level</p>
<p>					    Aug 10</p>
<p> Avg sugar content (pct)	     11.6		 12.0</p>
<p> Root weight (grams)		    270		  234</p>
<p> Daily root growth (grams)	    6.5		  6.0</p>
<p>The organisation did not give fresh data on the number of beets per hectare. The next time such data would appear would be on August 20, Rossakhsvyokla has said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
